-- title:
--   Every rational geometric place reduces to the reduction of a selected cusp
-- statement:
--   Let $D_2$ be a level-$25$ reduction datum at $2$, and let $P$ be a degree-one geometric place fixed by arithmetic Galois. Then there exists a selected geometric cusp $p_i^G$ with the same reduced place:
--
--   $$∃i∈Fin(5),\quad red_{D_2}(P)=red_{D_2}(p_i^G).$$
--
--   This narrows every rational reduction to one of the five explicitly controlled cusp reductions.
-- source:
--   B. Mazur, Modular curves and the Eisenstein ideal, Publ. IHES 47 (1977); Lean formalization of the order-25 case for this mission. Modules in the MazurProof/Keystone/Tate families are adapted from anthropics/fermats-last-theorem (Apache-2.0) via the xiangyazi24/FLT fork.

